#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "With --json, a command prints one JSON object on standard output; `status --follow --json` prints one per line. Fields are only ever added, never renamed or removed. Errors go to standard error as text, with the exit status below."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "Without a value, shows the volume. A number from 0 to 100 sets it; +N or -N changes it by N."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "`sona` starts Sona, or brings the running one to the front. Apple Music links among the arguments open in it. --hidden starts it without a window (playback, media keys and the tray only), as the start-at-login entry does. --version prints the version."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "`status --format TEMPLATE` prints each status through a Go text/template whose fields are the JSON fields (`{{.state}}`, `{{with .track}}{{.artist}} – {{.title}}{{end}}`, `{{.volume}}`); `{{json .x}}` quotes a value as JSON and `{{clock .position}}` writes seconds as m:ss. With --follow it suits Waybar's and Polybar's custom modules."
msgstr ""

